stem:
Nitric acid, $\text{HNO}_3$, can be made by reacting nitrogen dioxide with water.

The enthalpy change for the reaction can be measured indirectly using a Hess' cycle.

{{figure:pdf_visual_01.png}}

parts.text:
Complete the Hess' cycle using the values given in the table and hence calculate the enthalpy change, $\Delta H_\text{r}$, for this reaction.

Show your working.

{{figure:pdf_visual_02.png}}
